          "text": "# AI SDK v6: Key Features for LLM Architecture\n\nBased on the documentation, here are the primary capabilities:\n\n## Core Functionality\n\n**AI SDK Core** provides a unified API for generating text, structured objects, and tool calls with LLMs. **AI SDK UI** offers framework-agnostic hooks for building chat and generative interfaces.\n\n## Message & Conversation Management\n\nThe SDK supports \"chatbot message persistence\" and \"resume streams,\" enabling developers to maintain conversation history across sessions. Built-in hooks like `useChat` facilitate multi-turn interactions.\n\n## Tool Calling & Results\n\nThe system handles \"tool calling\" and \"tool result handling\" natively. Features include \"tool usage\" tracking and \"multi-step tools\" that \"handle multiple tool steps automatically,\" streamlining agent workflows.\n\n## Streaming Capabilities\n\nThe platform emphasizes streaming throughout—from text generation to custom data. Capabilities include \"streaming custom data\" and protocol-level support for progressive response delivery, reducing latency in client-server interactions.\n\n## State Management\n\nFeatures like \"message metadata\" and \"reading UIMessage streams\" provide granular control over conversation state. The SDK enables \"configuring call options\" for flexible request handling.\n\n## Multi-Turn Conversation Support\n\n\"Chatbot tool usage\" explicitly handles agent-based workflows. The system processes tool invocations, results, and subsequent model calls in unified patterns, ideal for complex multi-step interactions.\n\n## Simplified Architecture\n\nThese abstractions reduce boilerplate by standardizing provider integration, eliminating repetitive serialization logic, and consolidating streaming protocols—enabling cleaner client-server-LLM coordination.",
