          "text": "# AI SDK Core: generateText Function Guide\n\nBased on the documentation, here's what you need to know about `generateText`:\n\n## Basic Functionality\n\nThe `generateText` function generates text for a prompt and model synchronously. It's ideal for non-interactive use cases like drafting emails or summarizing content, and works well with agents using tools.\n\n## Response Object Contents\n\nAfter execution, the result contains several properties:\n\n- **text**: The generated text\n- **finishReason**: Why the model stopped generating\n- **usage**: Token consumption for the final step\n- **totalUsage**: Token count across all steps (for multi-step operations)\n- **toolCalls**: Tool calls made in the last step\n- **toolResults**: Results from those tool calls\n- **response**: Additional response info including messages and headers\n\n## Tool Execution & maxSteps\n\nWhile the documentation page focuses on basic text generation, it references that advanced features like \"tool calling and structured data generation are built on top of text generation.\" The framework supports multiple steps for tool execution, tracked via `totalUsage` and `steps` properties that reveal intermediate results.\n\n## Conversation State Management\n\nYou access raw response data—including headers and body—through `result.response`, enabling custom state tracking between calls. The `onFinish` callback receives generated messages via `response.messages`, supporting conversation history management.\n\n## Best Practice\n\nThe documentation emphasizes combining `generateText` with system prompts for refined behavior: *\"You can use more advanced prompts to generate text with more complex instructions.\"*",
