          "text": "# Tool Calling in AI SDK Core\n\n## Tool Call Structure\n\nTools in AI SDK Core contain three essential components: a **description** influencing tool selection, an **inputSchema** (Zod or JSON schema) consumed by the LLM for validation, and an optional **execute** function returning a generic RESULT type.\n\nTool calls receive a **toolCallId** as a second parameter in the execute function, enabling developers to track and reference specific invocations when streaming tool-call-related information.\n\n## Result Handling & Validation\n\nThe SDK automatically validates tool call inputs against defined schemas. When validation fails, it throws `InvalidToolInputError`. Tool execution errors are captured as `tool-error` content parts, enabling the LLM to attempt automatic fixes in multi-step scenarios rather than failing completely.\n\n## Multi-Step Execution\n\nUsing the `stopWhen` setting enables sequential tool calling: \"the model may need to call a tool to get the information it needs to answer your question where each generation (tool call or text generation) is a step.\"\n\nThe `steps` property contains all intermediate results. Developers can implement `onStepFinish` callbacks to execute logic after each step completes, or use `prepareStep` to customize behavior per iteration.\n\n## Message Context in Tools\n\nTool execute functions receive the messages sent to the LLM initiating the response, including \"the text, tool calls, and tool results from all previous steps\" in multi-step scenarios.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Dynamic tools** support unknown input/output types via `dynamicTool`\n- **Preliminary results** stream status updates using generator functions\n- **Response messages** are automatically provided for conversation history updates",
