          "text": "# streamText Function Overview\n\n## Message & Conversation History Handling\nThe `streamText` function accepts a `prompt` parameter and optional `system` message. It doesn't inherently manage conversation history—you must pass the complete message array to maintain context across interactions.\n\n## Available Event Types\nThe `fullStream` property provides comprehensive event access including:\n- `text-delta` and `text-start`/`text-end` for text chunks\n- `reasoning-delta` for model reasoning\n- `tool-call` for function invocations\n- `tool-input-delta` for streaming tool parameters\n- `tool-result` for execution results\n- `finish-step` and `finish` for completion markers\n\n## Tool Call Streaming\nTools execute during streaming and emit discrete events. The stream includes `tool-call` events with tool names, followed by `tool-input-delta` events showing parameter construction, then `tool-result` events with outcomes.\n\n## State Management Between Chunks\nState persists through promises that resolve when streaming completes: `result.text`, `result.toolCalls`, `result.usage`, and others accumulate across all chunks. Backpressure ensures tokens generate only when consumed.\n\n## Stream Conversion Formats\nThe function provides helper methods: `toUIMessageStreamResponse()` for Next.js API routes, `toTextStreamResponse()` for plain text, and `pipeTextStreamToResponse()` for Node.js response objects.",
