ait chatStorage.loadChatMessages(mostRecentChatId);\nclientRef.current.loadMessages(loadedMessages); // No sanitization!\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🏗️ Current Architecture Complexity\n\nYour architecture has **triple message history tracking**:\n\n1. **Client:** `UseAIClient._messages` (for sending to server)\n2. **Server AG-UI:** `ClientSession.messages` (AG-UI event format)\n3. **Server AI SDK:** `ClientSession.conversationHistory` (CoreMessage format for AI SDK)\n\n**Additional complexity:**\n- `currentChatId` (UI state) vs `threadId` (session identifier) can get out of sync\n- Manual sanitization required to strip provider-specific fields\n- Complex threadId-based history reset logic\n- `pendingChatId` pattern to prevent race conditions during chat switches\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Simplification Opportunities Using AI SDK\n\nAfter reviewing AI SDK v6 docs and your current implementation, here are the key opportunities:\n\n### What AI SDK Already Provides (You're Using v4)\n✅ Multi-step tool execution (`maxSteps: 10`)  \n✅ Automatic tool call/result handling  \n✅ Full conversation history in `result.response.messages`  \n✅ Native streaming with event types\n\n### What You're Still Doing Manually\n❌ Maintaining dual message formats (AG-UI + CoreMessage)  \n❌ Manual message sanitization  \n❌ Complex threadId synchronization  \n❌ Triple history tracking\n\n### AI SDK v6 Improvements\nThe upgrade from v4 → v6 won't drastically simplify architecture (you're already using most features), but offers:\n- Better TypeScript types\n- Improved streaming APIs\n- Enhanced error handling\n- More consistent tool handling\n\n**Recommendation:** Focus on fixing bugs and simplifying state management first, then consider v6 upgrade as a nice-to-have.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Proposed Change Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Fix Critical Bugs (High Priority)\n\n#### 1.1 Fix History Bleeding - Add `resetThreadId()` Method\n\n**File:** `packages/client/src/client.ts`\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Resets the thread ID when switchi